<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
	<Task>
		<Title>Assign Role Mapping &#8212; Operator Role Group (__ROLE__)</Title>
		<Description><![CDATA[<P>Endpoint task for the <B>Operator-Role-Group</B> assignment model. It ensures a named
user exists in the local <CODE>RoleAwareness.db</CODE> <CODE>Users</CODE> table and upserts a
<CODE>UserID -&gt; Role</CODE> row into the <CODE>Map</CODE> table.</P>

<H3>How it is used</H3>
<OL>
<LI>An automatic Computer Group is created per role. Its membership relevance carries the list
of operator usernames that hold the role and admits a device only when <B>exactly one</B> logged-on
user is in that list.</LI>
<LI>One <B>policy action</B> from this task is targeted at that group, with reapplication enabled
(e.g. reapply while relevant, every 1 day) so a host where nobody logs off still re-maps.</LI>
<LI>The ActionScript resolves the single matching user from client relevance and passes it as
<CODE>-UserName</CODE>. The script trusts its inputs &mdash; it does no logged-on-user parsing of its own.</LI>
<LI>The upsert uses the D-12 discipline &mdash; INSERT OR IGNORE plus a conditional UPDATE guarded by
<CODE>Locked_by_Override = 0</CODE> &mdash; and stamps <CODE>Assigned_By</CODE> with the issuing operator.</LI>
</OL>

<H3>Token substitution (per role)</H3>
<P>Like <CODE>bes/RoleRef-Policy-template.bes</CODE>, this file is a template. The group/action
generator replaces these tokens before PUT/POST:</P>
<UL>
<LI><CODE>__ROLE__</CODE> &mdash; the role name, e.g. <CODE>IT Operations</CODE></LI>
<LI><CODE>__USERNAME__</CODE> &mdash; the single user to map (bare sAMAccountName). Typically substituted
from client relevance in the ActionScript rather than baked in &mdash; see the parameter line below.</LI>
<LI><CODE>__ASSIGNED_BY__</CODE> &mdash; the operator who issued the task.</LI>
</UL>

<H3>Prerequisites</H3>
<P>The endpoint must already have been initialised by the &quot;Init  Current User and UserRole DB&quot;
task (787): <CODE>RoleAwareness.db</CODE>, <CODE>Sqlite-Helper.ps1</CODE> and <CODE>sqlite3.exe</CODE> in place. The
&lt;Relevance&gt; below gates on all three. <CODE>scripts/Assign-RoleMapping.ps1</CODE> must be staged in the
Custom Repository at <CODE>Uploads/CustomRepository/SoftwarePortal/rolegroups/</CODE> and the prefetch
<CODE>sha1:</CODE>/<CODE>size:</CODE> re-pinned whenever that script changes.</P>

<H3>Scope / revoke</H3>
<P>v1 maps on single-user devices only (enforced by the Computer Group relevance). There is no
revoke &mdash; loss of the operator role removes the device from the group, the policy action stops
applying, and the row lapses at <CODE>Valid_to</CODE> (age-out).</P>]]></Description>
		<Relevance><![CDATA[windows of operating system]]></Relevance>
		<Relevance><![CDATA[number of logged on users = 1]]></Relevance>
		<Relevance><![CDATA[(exists file (it &amp; "\EC\SoftwarePortal\RoleAwareness.db") AND exists file (it &amp; "\EC\SoftwarePortal\Sqlite-Helper.ps1") AND exists file (it &amp; "\EC\sqlite\sqlite3.exe")) of (pathname of parent folder of parent folder of client folder of site "actionsite")]]></Relevance>
		<Category></Category>
		<Source>Internal</Source>
		<SourceID></SourceID>
		<SourceReleaseDate>2026-09-09</SourceReleaseDate>
		<SourceSeverity></SourceSeverity>
		<CVENames></CVENames>
		<SANSID></SANSID>
		<MIMEField>
			<Name>x-fixlet-modification-time</Name>
			<Value>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</Value>
		</MIMEField>
		<Domain>BESC</Domain>
		<DefaultAction ID="Action1">
			<Description>
				<PreLink>Click </PreLink>
				<Link>here</Link>
				<PostLink> to map role "__ROLE__" to the target user.</PostLink>
			</Description>
			<ActionScript MIMEType="application/x-Fixlet-Windows-Shell"><![CDATA[begin prefetch block
	add prefetch item name=Assign-RoleMapping.ps1 sha1=f3afb1535c616ed54aa0e6fc9e7bce94cde8fed3 size=9086 url=http://127.0.0.1:{maximum of (it as integer) of (((value "port" of key "HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Wow6432Node\BigFix\Enterprise Server" of registry)as string) |"0"; ((preceding text of first "/" of following text of first ":" of following text of first ":" of it ) of (( value "ClientRegistration URL" of key "HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\WOW6432Node\BigFix\Enterprise Server\GatherService" of registry) as string))|"0";"52311")}/Uploads/CustomRepository/SoftwarePortal/rolegroups/Assign-RoleMapping.ps1 sha256=fff2a3d89c7fe0392f81035b35133e4326eabcdb22d39ff874d05eea1e08669b
end prefetch block

// Client-relevance substitutions -- NOT touched by any brace-escaping pass (script is
// prefetched, not createfile'd, so no { -> {{ escaping is needed anywhere in this action).
	parameter "SWPDir"="{(concatenation (if windows of operating system then "\" else "/") of ((item 0 of it;item 1 of it;item 2 of it) of ((pathname of parent folder of parent folder of client folder of site "actionsite") as string,"EC","SoftwarePortal")))}"
	parameter "SQLiteDir"="{(concatenation (if windows of operating system then "\" else "/") of ((item 0 of it;item 1 of it;item 2 of it) of ((pathname of parent folder of parent folder of client folder of site "actionsite") as string,"EC","sqlite")))}"
	parameter "TargetStore"="{(concatenation (if windows of operating system then "\" else "/") of ((item 0 of it;item 1 of it;item 2 of it;item 3 of it) of ((pathname of parent folder of parent folder of client folder of site "actionsite") as string,"EC","SoftwarePortal","RoleAwareness.db")))}"

// Inputs. Role and Assigned_By are per-action tokens. UserName is the single logged-on
// user. "name of current user" was tried first and found to error on several live
// endpoints (DC01/GPBFS/PROXDEV11 and others) -- that inspector depends on session/
// console-ownership state and can be unresolvable even when exactly one user is
// logged on. "concatenation of (names of logged on users)" never errors: it collapses
// to the single username when there's exactly one (the only case the Computer Group's
// own membership relevance is designed to admit -- reinforced by the "number of logged
// on users = 1" gate above) and to an empty string if there are zero, which
// Assign-RoleMapping.ps1 already handles as a clean [ABORT] rather than a crash.
	parameter "Role"="__ROLE__"
	parameter "AssignedBy"="__ASSIGNED_BY__"
	parameter "UserName"="{concatenation "" of (names of logged on users as lowercase)}"

// Land the endpoint script next to RoleAwareness.db.
	if {not exists folder ((parameter "SWPDir") & "\rolegroups")}
		runhidden cmd /c mkdir "{parameter "SWPDir"}\rolegroups"
	endif
	delete "{parameter "SWPDir"}\rolegroups\Assign-RoleMapping.ps1"
	copy "__Download\Assign-RoleMapping.ps1" "{parameter "SWPDir"}\rolegroups\Assign-RoleMapping.ps1"

	action uses wow64 redirection {x64 of operating system}
	waithidden powershell.exe -NonInteractive -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "{parameter "SWPDir"}\rolegroups\Assign-RoleMapping.ps1" -Role "{parameter "Role"}" -UserName "{parameter "UserName"}" -AssignedBy "{parameter "AssignedBy"}" -SQLDir "{parameter "SQLiteDir"}" -DatabasePath "{parameter "TargetStore"}" -SqliteHelperPath "{parameter "SWPDir"}\Sqlite-Helper.ps1"
]]></ActionScript>
		</DefaultAction>
	</Task>
</BES>
